    npcIcons["Ajido-Marujido"].note = "Involved in Quests:\
* I Can Hear a Rainbow\
* Wonder Wands\
\
Involved in Missions:\
* Windurst Mission 1-1: The Horutoto Ruins Experiment\
* Windurst Mission 2-1: Lost for Words\
* Windurst Mission 3-1: To Each His Own Right\
* Windurst Mission 3-2: Written in the Stars\
* San d'Oria Mission 4-1: Magicite\
* Bastok Mission 4-1: Magicite\
* Windurst Mission 4-1: Magicite\
* Windurst Mission 6-1: Full Moon Fountain\
* Windurst Mission 8-2: The Jester Who'd Be King\
* Windurst Mission 9-1: Doll of the Dead\
* Windurst Mission 9-2: Moon Reading\
\
Notes:\
Biography: Ajido-Marujido is the \"rogue\" Minister of Windurst's Orastery, the Ministry of Windurst that oversees the use of magic and the training of mages. He is also the son of the creator of the Cardians and the former Minister of the Manustery Zonpa-Zippa, and is the brother of current Manustery Minister Apururu. Although a very powerful mage and a well-respected public figure, he is always getting himself or a random adventurer into trouble in his pursuit for the truth about Windurst and its past. Although labeled as unpredictable and a rogue, he cares deeply about the future of Windurst and its well-being, even more so than his reputation and his political career. He is introduced to us as a \"Child Genius\" student in one of the early Wings of the Goddess missions. Even then he has a flair for getting himself, and you, into trouble. He later becomes one of Shantotto's pupils prior to his role of minister of the Orastery Battle NPC: Ajido-Marujido fights alongside the party during the battlefield event at Full Moon Fountain for Windurst Mission 9-2: Moon Reading. He fights in the second round of the battle, versus Vyala and Tatzlwurm. Ajido-Marujido must be kept alive, because if he falls the battle will be considered a loss; and since he has low HP and grabs enmity very easily with his powerful spells, it's important to keep the heat off him. Ajido can cast all ancient magic, uses both Chainspell and Manafont, teleports around the arena, and has an unusual hand-to-hand attack style similar to Mammets."
