* Achieving True Power\
\
Involved in Quests:\
* Puppetmaster Blues\
\
Notes:\
Dialogue: Under level 30 chat ------------------- Shamarhaan : ... Valkeng : Dancing now. Please observe. Over level 30 chat ------------------- Valkeng : Would like to join in dance? Shamarhaan : Looks like he's taken a liking to you! Shamarhaan : This little guy's name is Valkeng. What do you say, Val? Valkeng : Nice to meet kind sir. Shamarhaan : Ha ha, isn't he just the cutest thing? Shamarhaan : But to tell the truth, it's only because I made him that way. I'm not sure if you noticed, but I was controlling his every movement! Shamarhaan : 'Puppets' like him are called automatons. They can do all sorts of things, but it all depends on the handler's skill. Shamarhaan : I make my living entertaining people this way. Shamarhaan : People who can control and customize automatons are referred to as 'puppetmasters' in the Near East. Shamarhaan : You say you'd like to give it a try yourself? Shamarhaan : Ha ha, I'm afraid you've got to be a puppetmaster for that. Shamarhaan : Eh? You want to be a puppetmaster, do you? Quite the hasty one, aren't we? Shamarhaan : Well, if I had time, I'd be glad to teach you the ropes, but I can't make a living staying in the same town for months on end, now can I? Shamarhaan : Ah, I have the perfect solution! You should meet with my pupil, Iruki-Waraki. I've taught him everything I know. Shamarhaan : Not only that, but he's currently the most acclaimed puppeteer in Vana'diel! You should be able to find him entertaining the folk in Aht Urhgan Whitegate with his automaton. Shamarhaan : He has grown far better than I. You really must witness his expertise before learning how to control an automaton yourself. Followup chat ------------------- Shamarhaan : If you really want to become a puppetmaster, I advise speaking to Iruki-Waraki in Aht Urhgan Whitegate."
